# TypeScript Rules

Strict TypeScript — prefer explicit domain types in `src/types/`.

## Domain Types

```ts
// Insight / blog
import type { Article } from "@/types/article"

// Portfolio & ads
import type { WebWork } from "@/types/web-work"
import type { Ad } from "@/types/ad"

// ✅ Props eksplisit
interface NewsCardProps {
  article: Article
}

// ✅ unknown + validate, bukan any — terutama API / Sheets rows
function mapSheetRow(raw: unknown): Article { ... }
```

## Naming
- Components → PascalCase file · Hooks → `useXxx.ts` · Utils → camelCase
- Constants → `SCREAMING_SNAKE` · Types → PascalCase
- Data helpers → verb + noun: `getArticles`, `getArticleBySlug`

## Data & forms
- Sheets / mail / slug / date helpers live in `src/lib/`
- Public mutations go through `src/app/api/**` route handlers when that's the existing pattern
- Don't introduce Zustand / TanStack Query for static or server-fetched marketing data unless needed
